    "interpretation": "For polyhedra whose faces are lattice-representable planes the area error is purely an edge/corner artefact (marching cubes chamfers convex edges) and decays as O(1/rho) to ZERO -- halving on every doubling of rho. A convergent regime therefore exists. The sphere does not enter it: its error converges to a non-zero limit. The sphere/ellipsoid error is consequently an orientation-dependent asymptotic bias, not insufficient resolution."
  },
